.Dd November 16, 2026
.Dt ID 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm id
.Nd print account and group identities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl u | Fl g | Fl G
.Op Fl n
.Op Ar user
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
reads
.Pa /etc/passwd
and
.Pa /etc/group
and prints the selected identity for
.Ar user ,
or for the caller when no operand is given.
The full form is
.Dl uid=N(name) gid=N(name) groups=N(name),...
.Pp
The
.Fl u
option selects the effective uid,
.Fl g
the effective gid, and
.Fl G
all groups.
.Fl n
prints names instead of numbers and requires one of the selectors.
.Pp
The kernel is root-only in 0.2.0, so the caller identity is root. U3 supplies the real
effective uid.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/passwd -compact
.It Pa /etc/passwd
account records
.It Pa /etc/group
group records
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
An unknown account exits with status 1; a usage error exits with status 2.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr whoami 1 ,
.Xr groupadd 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD.
